---
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import GenerationLossSimulator from "../../components/GenerationLossSimulator.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../../site-config";

// Root-absolute hrefs written by hand in an .astro file skip Astro base
// handling: they work on localhost and 404 on the deployed path.
const week1Href = `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}sessions/01-photocopy/`;
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Generation-loss simulator"
  description="Watch text degrade across repeated copies, and see why the same settings never produce the same result twice."
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <p class="lede">
    Week 1 asked you to count how a copy becomes harder to read, and drew a
    careful line between three claims: the counting rule is deterministic,
    your own repeatability is something you can check, and two readers still
    disagree because resolving a damaged mark is an interpretation. This page
    runs the same rule on text instead of a scanned card, so you can watch
    generation loss compound in real time, and re-run the same settings to
    see that the <em>outcome</em> is not deterministic even though the
    <em>counting</em> is.
  </p>

  <GenerationLossSimulator />

  <p>
    See <a href={week1Href}>Week 1: The office that ate itself</a>{" "}
    for the graded activity this page supplements — it does not replace the
    pack, the worksheet or the worked answer.
  </p>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
</style>
